# tally 2.1.8 R15, L §5.18, §5.10 (T's STOP-REPORT 7, unit/probes/ask/ASK-02): value of a place valued whole is its
# price at d, so it passes the price on unchanged and under partial its hole stays linear: v1 is 100.00 DUK + 1 x the
# car's hole, scaled by a known share in v2. Without partial (v3) the line is the hole. db8894ca printed v1 plain.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2025-06-30
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

place car: assets DUK priced car_value lives 2025-01-01..

input car_value: money DUK question "What is the car worth?"
input extra: money DUK
input share: num

ask v1: value(car, 2025-06-30) in DUK + extra partial
ask v2: share * (value(car, 2025-06-30) in DUK) partial
ask v3: value(car, 2025-06-30) in DUK + extra

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  car_value = ?"What is the car worth?" "none"
  extra = 100.00 DUK "s"
  share = 0.5 "s"
=== expect
v1: 100.00 DUK + 1 × ?"What is the car worth?" (car_value)
  cut 2025-06-30
v2: 0.5 × ?"What is the car worth?" (car_value)
  cut 2025-06-30
v3: ?"What is the car worth?" (car_value)
  cut 2025-06-30
